This scene is benched in ADVISORY mode: bench.py prints its accuracy but does
NOT fail CI on a miss, and it is kept out of baseline.json.

Why: player_stats_chat reads free-form, human-typed alliance-chat messages
(labeled/unlabeled/mixed-order stats, Cyrillic/Japanese/emoji handles, avatar
frames and translator badges bleeding into the text layer, typos, and prose
corrections). Measured on these fixtures the parser reaches:

    name 81.8%   attack 90.9%   hp 81.8%   defense 81.8%

against targets of 90% / 95% / 95% / 95%. Every remaining miss is OCR
destroying the source line outright — a whole "1) 407" reduced to "(ay: —", a
handle reduced to "A > №" — not a parsing bug that more code would fix. Gating
on this would make CI flaky without signalling a real regression.

The value of these fixtures is coverage: they exercise the full-image OCR +
state-machine path end-to-end on real screenshots — the one dashboard data type
that previously had zero real-image bench coverage (only mocked unit tests).
Row counts now match the goldens exactly, so a future regression shows up as a
falling percentage rather than as a misalignment cascade.

To promote this scene to blocking once the parser reaches its targets: delete
this marker file, then run `uv run python ../../tools/bench-ocr/bench.py
--write-baseline` from tracker/apps/ocr-service so the scene enters baseline.json.
